    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0102" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg60"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 27</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.00/10–2951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting United States Special Representative in
                        Europe (</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Riddleberger</hi><hi rendition="#italic">) to the Acting
                        Administrator for Economic Cooperation (</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Bissell</hi><hi rendition="#italic">)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-29T13:00:00+01:00">October 29, 1951—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Repto 5428. Personal for Harriman, Bissell and Porter, from Tasca and Gordon.
                    Tasca met Saturday afternoon with Hall Patch, Chairman of Executive Committee
                    OEEC, and Sperienburg, Chairman of Council at official level. Both officials
                    stated time had come to put real steam behind OEEC manifesto. Under procedures
                    agreed by Council, OEEC will set up high level working parties on coal, steel,
                    electric power, as well as agriculture and manpower. Housing will await
                    Secretariat study. Procedure for manpower is under discussion.</p>
                <p>Hall-Patch would like to get really high level people on working party on coal,
                    steel and power. He and Sperienburg are most anxious to have top level Americans
                    participate. Examples would be Clarence Randall on steel, Robert Koenig on coal,
                    Walter [<hi rendition="#italic">Walker</hi>] Cisler on power.</p>
                <p>High level working parties are to report to vertical country committees by
                    November 25 for comment and council December 15.</p>
                <p>Strongly urge cooperation with OEEC on this matter. If you agree, US experts
                    should come as soon as possible to Paris. [Tasca and Gordon.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Riddleberger</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
